    "description": "## Summary\n\nWhenever a Player's Player_Status\\__c changes — from any source: manual UI edit, screen flow, record-triggered or scheduled automation, or data load — the system stamps Player_Status_Set_Datec and Player_Status_Last_Updated_By_\\_c.\n\n## Context\n\nEvery other story in this epic (BUILD-178) writes Player status, and statuses can also change by hand (e.g., the unban path in BUILD-255) or via data updates. Rather than each automation stamping audit fields itself — and manual edits slipping through unstamped — one before-save flow on Account owns the stamping for every path. The other children rely on this story and do no stamping of their own.\n\n## Current state\n\nPlayer_Status_Set_Date\\__c (DateTime) exists. Player_Status_Last_Updated_By_\\_c exists as a **Lookup(User)** — a lookup is unnecessary for an audit field and will be replaced with Text. Lookup fields cannot be converted in place; the field must be deleted and recreated.\n\n## Proposed solution\n\n1. REPLACE Account.Player_Status_Last_Updated_By__c: delete the Lookup(User) field (currently unpopulated) and recreate it as **Text**, same label (\"Status Last Updated By\"), read-only on layouts.\n2. NEW before-save record-triggered flow Account_Before_Save_Stamp_Player_Status_Audit — entry: Player record type AND Player_Status\\__c changed. Stamps Player_Status_Set_Datec = now and Player_Status_Last_Updated_By_\\_c = the running user's name. Automated contexts (e.g., the BUILD-254 scheduled flow) will stamp \"Automated Process\" — this is expected and desirable for the audit trail.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. A status change via manual UI edit, screen flow, record-triggered flow, scheduled flow, or data load stamps both fields.\n2. Account edits that do not change Player_Status__c leave both fields untouched.\n3. Scheduled/automated status changes stamp \"Automated Process\" as the updater.\n4. Bulk-safe at 200+ records.\n\n## Output\n\nRecreated field + flow deployed in Partial SB; API names recorded on this ticket; requirements doc updated.",
